# Every harness dejima supports, and every one under assessment, so a session
# working on this repo can run and test the integration rather than reason
# about it. A harness dejima claims to support and cannot exercise here is one
# whose guards are asserted rather than observed.
#
# claude-code is not listed: like every supported harness it installs from its
# own manifest's `install` spec, into a layer of its own above the base image.
# Nothing here has to name it.
npm:opencode-ai

# The second supported harness. Listed here even though it installs from its
# own manifest like claude-code does, because that spec only puts it in the
# image when it is the SELECTED harness - and a session working on dejima runs
# one harness while needing to exercise the other.
#
# Needs AVX2: its CLI is a Bun-embedded compiled binary and Bun's default build
# requires it, so a VM whose CPU model is x86-64-v2-AES - Proxmox's default for
# new guests - gets SIGILL before any output, and no baseline build is
# published. x86-64-v3 or better is the requirement, and it is a property of
# the VM rather than of dejima. See docs/development.md, "Worked example:
# Cline".
#
# No allowed-domains entry accompanies this, unlike opencode: Cline fetches no
# provider catalogue at startup. Its own hosted endpoints (api.cline.bot,
# app.cline.bot, otel.cline.bot) are deliberately absent for the same reason
# the model API is - a name granted by being written here is a name nobody
# reviewed, and the point is to point it at an endpoint of our choosing.
npm:cline

apt:tmux
apt:bats
# The other half of what CI runs. The CI job installs it itself, so without
# this line a sandbox is the one place the gate cannot be run at all - and a
# base image that happens to carry it is not a guarantee, as one that stopped
# carrying it demonstrated.
apt:shellcheck
